 chase serrano through the ship while  also dealing with some final echo  soldiers until we make it to him again  trishka discovers the truth about her  father ishii gets killed and we attempt  to kill serrano ourselves  of course nothing goes grayson's way as  apparently serrano is  alive trishka and grayson then make it  to the last escape pod before the bomb  blows off and the game  ends we don't get to kill serrano but we  do get to escape the planet  we also get a small ending cutscene that  shows that ishii is still alive thanks  to the ai and some medical attention  it would be a fairly interesting ending  if this game wasn't 10 years old  it's clear this game hasn't gotten a  sequel since then so we really don't  know what exactly happened  i'm assuming the devs did this to have a  backup plan in case things blew up and  got a ton of sales but it doesn't seem  like that's the case  after doing a small bit of research it  does seem the developers people can fly  were then assigned to gears of war  judgment under the orders of epic games  they then eventually became an  independent company in 2015 and then  said that they wanted to give the series  a second life and an attempt to make it  more popular they did make a remastered  version of the game bullet stormfall  clip and it did prove to the team that  the game is quite popular and that there  may be a chance for a sequel in the  future for now though who knows what's  going to happen  once you beat the campaign though you  can do the overkill version we discussed  before but  what else is there to do well the game  did have multiplayer but it's not as  popular as it used to be  i couldn't find a match after searching  for a while so i decided to look up some  footage myself and it seems to be a  horde mode style  game where you reach a certain amount of  points within a certain amount of  enemies  if you don't reach the point threshold  then you lose other than that you can  always do the echoes there are two  different versions of these echoes the  normal echoes and the ultimate echoes  these are challenge runs through the  areas of the campaign the normal echoes  are quite easy although you do have  limited ammo and equipment but can  refill them at drop kits this is where  that knowledge of the game comes in is  you have to be crafty with your kills or  you'll end up missing out on easy points  the ultimate echoes are a little bit  more challenging giving you one  then two then three separate challenges  to accomplish before you're finished  with the area afterwards you can  officially begin the actual challenge  since it now tracks your score for the  leaderboard so you're essentially doing  four different echoes in one echo both  the normal echoes and ultimate echoes  have about three pages worth of content  which arguably may take you just as long  as the campaign itself  and i've always found that i like these  things but only for a while  it's more just a personal thing for me  i've never fully completed the  challenges in arkham knight or  dishonored i just do a few and that's  really about it  you may feel different about it but it's  never hooked me in as much as maybe some  other players  the very very very last thing in this  game that's specific to the full clip  version of the game  is the duke nukem bundle which swaps a  grayson for duke nukem and he's actually  fully voiced  listen up robot dude get your head out  of your ass  and get your [ __ ] together capisce  let's get back to it it's a pretty cool  dlc and for five dollars you can't go  wrong especially if you're a fan of duke  nukem  buttstorm is such a distinctive game i  can't really think of any game in recent  years that did the things this game did  from its dialogue to its skill shots  it made the player want to use all the  weapons and make them try new things  it teaches the player that being  comfortable can be boring i found myself  having more fun when i was actually  trying to get new challenges done even  if it was infuriating to do  it was much better than just running  around with the three specific guns for  a majority of the game and this is  reinforced by the placement of these  guns like we talked about before  making it not feel overwhelming and  giving the player enough time to have  fun with these weapons and all the  possible skill shots with those weapons  it's a game i've played numerous times  and i'll probably be playing again in  the future because there's nothing like  it  with that however we have come to the  end of the video if you've liked the  video then be sure to give it a like  as always subscribe if you're new for  more video essay commentaries like this  one  if you're a returning subscriber i thank  you for coming back and  take care everyone have a good rest of  your day and goodbye  [Music]  you
 

